From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:17:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] r4 journey fix 4: island sky dome follows the lakeside
 sky zenith/low (linear), not the clear colour

The dome/cloud follow target during the island->lakeside blend was the
lakeside clear colour (#1c8fb8 by day). It now reads
lakesideModeLighting(mode).waterSkyZenithLinear and waterSkyLowLinear
(read-only; never waterSkyHorizonLinear, the reflected olive shore):
lakesideSkyDomeTargetLinear(mode) = their mean (one mainColor tint per mesh;
the dome's vertex gradient keeps its shape), handed to skyFollow through
skyFollowTargetFromLinear (exact inverse of srgb8ToLinear, no rounding).
SKY_FOLLOW_MAX_GAIN 8 -> 12: the day target needs 9.57 on the real dome's red.
The island props still fade out over w 0.6-0.95, after which the sky is the
camera clear colour as before. lakesideModeLighting untouched.
Test: lakeside-sky-follow updated (target, zenith/low round trip, not Horizon,
real-mesh gains inside the clamp, night, toggle, wiring).
